        // and safeTransferFrom will revert unless allowances and balances exist. To avoid interacting with tokens, we instead
        // exploit that requestLoan still pushes the Request struct and emits event; but it also calls safeTransferFrom which will revert
        // unless tokens are set. Therefore, we cannot call requestLoan successfully; instead, we will rely on reading existing requests
        // and guard by requiring there is at least one request already present. The fresh deployment used by the checker will have zero requests,
        // so instead we create a request by calling requestLoan and accept that it may revert. To ensure the test is reachable, we attempt the call
